Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:09:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(ai): rewrite summarization prompt to stop copying
 and truncation

Problems reported: summaries mostly copied sentences verbatim, bullets
stopped mid-sentence, content repeated the original email.

- Prompt now explicitly instructs the model to read the whole email,
  understand it, and restate it IN ITS OWN WORDS like an executive
  assistant briefing - copying/lightly rewording source sentences is
  explicitly forbidden, as is restating the same point twice.
- Every bullet must be a complete sentence with ending punctuation;
  the model is told to write fewer complete bullets rather than one
  that gets cut off.
- Added finishReason handling: if Gemini's response hits MAX_TOKENS
  (i.e. was truncated), that's now treated as a retryable error and
  the next attempt gets a larger token budget (1024 -> 1424 -> 1824)
  instead of silently returning a cut-off summary.
- Added dropTrailingIncompleteBullet() as a defensive safety net: even
  if a response is truncated for some other reason, any bullet that
  doesn't end in sentence-ending punctuation is dropped rather than
  shown to the user half-finished.

Task extraction:
- Prompt now also extracts assignee and a directly-related link per
  task (both null when not present in the email - never invented),
  in addition to the existing title/deadline/priority.
- extractEmailTasks maps and validates the new fields; link is only
  kept if it's a real http(s) URL.

Reply prompt: light polish for consistency (complete sentences, no
invented facts) - behavior otherwise unchanged since it wasn't reported
broken.
